WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:02.060
- I'm hanging all hour with the host

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:05.402
of the #IMOMSOHARD podcast
Jen and Kristin, give it up.

00:00:05.402 --> 00:00:07.400
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.350
My next guest is an actress, model,

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:11.410
host of "So You Think You Can Dance?"

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.040
And of course, a mom.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.410
Her new children's book
is called "The Joy in You"

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.760
and it's out right now.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.080
Joining us all the way from London,

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.273
please welcome Cat Deeley everybody!

00:00:21.273 --> 00:00:26.180
(smooth music)
(audience cheers)

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.933
First of all I love your lip color.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.620
- You know what, I just
said to your producers,

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:32.750
is it too much?

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:33.750
Like--
- No!

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.420
- To me, this is such an
amazing occasion I've literally,

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.862
I've got a glass of champagne.

00:00:38.862 --> 00:00:39.695
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:39.695 --> 00:00:40.622
I've got my bottle.

00:00:40.622 --> 00:00:42.600
Like literally, I get to hang out

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.340
with cool, funny, smart moms.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.440
Like I haven't done this enough.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.585
So for me, that's enough of an excuse

00:00:49.585 --> 00:00:50.710
for a red lip.
- Oh I think--

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:51.785
Girl if I thought it was too much

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:52.760
I just wouldn't have talked about it.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.231
I think it's awesome. (Kelly laughs)

00:00:54.231 --> 00:00:56.280
I think it's beautiful.
- Thank you.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.113
- Yes.

00:00:57.113 --> 00:00:59.090
But Cat, tell us about
your new children's book.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:01.570
I read to my children,
no kidding every night.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:02.777
It's a huge thing in our household.

00:01:02.777 --> 00:01:06.183
I'm assuming it was inspired
by your boys, right?

00:01:06.183 --> 00:01:07.495
- Of course, course it was.

00:01:07.495 --> 00:01:09.220
You know what, it's one of these things

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:10.766
that I'd always wanted to do.

00:01:10.766 --> 00:01:12.853
It was a definitely an ambition.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.510
And then it got to a point
where I was like okay,

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:20.370
like any other mom, I'm sure
you completely understand,

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:22.860
at the end of the night I am exhausted.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.040
I put on my pajamas,

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.160
I can barely string a sentence together,

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.480
I'm completely inarticulate.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.390
And at that moment I'm putting them to bed

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.870
and I'm like okay,

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:35.963
what do I want to say when
I can't find the words?

00:01:37.378 --> 00:01:40.110
What feelings do I want my
children to go to bed with?

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.440
And I think it doesn't matter who you are

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.590
or what our background is,
or where you come from.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:48.250
Essentially we all want the
same thing for our children,

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.990
which is to be happy and kind.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:54.137
Everything else is great,
but we basically want that.

00:01:54.137 --> 00:01:56.550
And we want them to be able
to talk about their emotions

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.240
and talk about their feelings.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:01:59.490
And.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:02.030
I feel that's how they
reach their full potential

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:02.863
as an adult.

00:02:02.863 --> 00:02:05.270
So really it was all of those things.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.650
It's feelings, emotions, thoughts,

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:10.150
and it's top and tailed with love.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:13.430
And it's just how I want my
boys to go to bed at night.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:14.263
- I love it.

00:02:14.263 --> 00:02:16.162
I love the art as well.
(Jen cries)

00:02:16.162 --> 00:02:17.709
I know.
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:17.709 --> 00:02:20.170
We wanna read it too.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:24.440
No the art is so beautifully
done, I love the illustration.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:26.970
What do your kids think about the book?

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.100
Are they excited about it?

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.430
Like my girl didn't get it for a while

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:31.720
that it was named after her.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.490
Like I have one and she
didn't get it for a while.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:34.386
Now she thinks it's super cool.

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:36.770
But what do your kids think?

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:37.670
- Oh they didn't get it either.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:38.794
Like you get at the end of the book

00:02:38.794 --> 00:02:39.627
and he'd be like, why are you in the book?

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.479
- Why is your picture, yeah.

00:02:42.479 --> 00:02:45.990
- They didn't, yes,
exactly the same thing.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:47.331
Didn't get it at all.

00:02:47.331 --> 00:02:49.127
And then sometimes he'll be,

00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:52.080
Milo will be literally like hold my face,

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.870
and he'll do this thing where he holds it

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:55.150
and gives me a big smooch

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.417
and he goes "mom that
was a movie star kiss.

00:02:57.417 --> 00:03:00.000
"It's so lovely, I love this book."

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.510
And then other times, obviously
because he's a four-year-old

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.153
it's slightly Jekyll and Hyde,
and you never really know

00:03:06.153 --> 00:03:07.453
what you're gonna get right?
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:08.286
- Yes.
- You know that

00:03:08.286 --> 00:03:09.119
feeling right?
- Yes, amen.

00:03:09.119 --> 00:03:12.257
- And so the one night he says to me,

00:03:12.257 --> 00:03:15.437
"mom" and he's a bit like
a teenager at this point.

00:03:15.437 --> 00:03:18.680
"Mom, you know your book
it says I can do anything,"

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.017
and I says "yes Milo you can

00:03:20.017 --> 00:03:22.143
"if you put your mind to something

00:03:22.143 --> 00:03:23.897
"and you find something you love

00:03:23.897 --> 00:03:27.848
"and you wanna work hard, you
can do anything you wanna do."

00:03:27.848 --> 00:03:30.100
And he's like "well
that's not true is it?"

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.201
- Oh no.
- And I was like, uh.

00:03:32.201 --> 00:03:34.180
"Well what do you mean?"

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.057
He says, "well that's not true,

00:03:35.057 --> 00:03:36.787
"because what I wanna do

00:03:36.787 --> 00:03:39.337
"is I wanna take a
koala home from the zoo,

00:03:39.337 --> 00:03:41.107
"bring it here and keep it as a pet.

00:03:41.107 --> 00:03:42.993
"I can't do that can I mom?"
(audience laughs)

00:03:42.993 --> 00:03:45.222
- He's very literal.

00:03:45.222 --> 00:03:46.270
- And through my head I'm going,

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:50.646
Cat Deeley's kid kidnaps
koala and kills it from zoo,

00:03:50.646 --> 00:03:52.033
you know like I'm thinking that.

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:53.984
And I'm like oh no no no no no no no no

00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:55.940
you can't do that, you can't do that.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.577
I said "but what you can do"

00:03:57.577 --> 00:03:58.460
and you know in those,

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.053
and I'm sure we've all had those moments,

00:04:00.053 --> 00:04:02.960
where you know when they ask you something

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.390
and your brain is like racing

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:06.420
trying to find the right answer.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.490
And you can almost hear your brain work?

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.747
And it's like (Cat rolls tongue)

00:04:10.747 --> 00:04:12.640
I mean it's almost like a drum roll

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.690
for when you come up with the answer.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.000
And you're going as fast as you can.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.700
And I said "no Milo you
absolutely can't do that."

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.401
I said "but what you can do,

00:04:20.401 --> 00:04:23.647
"is if you go to school
and you study really hard

00:04:23.647 --> 00:04:26.337
"and maybe you might study
something called biology.

00:04:26.337 --> 00:04:28.967
"And then you can study
something called zoology

00:04:28.967 --> 00:04:29.907
"and go to university.

00:04:29.907 --> 00:04:33.641
"Then you could be in charge
of all the koalas at the zoo.

00:04:33.641 --> 00:04:37.467
"Or you could even travel to
the other side of the planet,

00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:39.837
"which is as far as you
can get to Australia,

00:04:39.837 --> 00:04:41.957
"which is where koalas come from.

00:04:41.957 --> 00:04:43.717
"And you could go to a sanctuary,

00:04:43.717 --> 00:04:46.137
"and you could help koalas
who don't have a mom and dad.

00:04:46.137 --> 00:04:47.287
"And you could feed them--"
- Great answer.

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:48.947
- And I just.

00:04:48.947 --> 00:04:50.517
And I left it like that.

00:04:50.517 --> 00:04:53.230
And in my head I was
like high fiving myself

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.063
and all the rest of it.

00:04:54.063 --> 00:04:55.535
And he just looked at me like that.

00:04:55.535 --> 00:04:56.400
(audience laughs)

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.219
- He's like, not the same.
- All right mom.

00:04:58.219 --> 00:04:59.134
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:59.134 --> 00:05:00.810
All right mom.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.510
- I guess I'll accept that answer.

00:05:04.007 --> 00:05:05.570
- Exactly.
- I love that.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.770
I love how you twisted,
that was really really nice.

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:11.470
Well Cat's new book "The
Joy in You" is out now,

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:12.707
you'll have to get it.

